n when determining how close each event pertained to the events listed by Clancy et al. [21], Within the inclusion bracket, there were 3 tiers that would determine if the region would be assigned a CL of 1, 2, or 3. The three tiers correspond to the three CLs where tier 1 is the most ambiguous verbiage, while tier 3 is the most clear and defined verbiage.\n\nLoretta Teresa Sutkus et al.\n\nDE GRUYTER", "width": 1654, "height": 2205, "blocks": [{"kind": "list", "text": "Proliferation peaks\" Region peaks*", "bbox": {"x": 744.2999898312668, "y": 941.7187481165627, "width": 59.72779530419247, "height": 197.5312499999998}}, {"kind": "heading", "text": "Table 1: Inclusion/exclusion criteria for literature review verbiage of neurodevelopmental events'", "bbox": {"x": 303.18517825746176, "y": 1129.926608155615, "width": 30.693520348601883, "height": 891.3954019546508}}, {"kind": "list", "text": "Early phase\" First element", "bbox": {"x": 466.09006489931414, "y": 1340.7755156466349, "width": 59.275797833336775, "height": 138.92205226421342}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Neural event", "bbox": {"x": 376.74443654691584, "y": 1888.0312486678126, "width": 22.972235367033225, "height": 133.21875000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Region appears or starts...", "bbox": {"x": 473.2277682371477, "y": 1846.687497817969, "width": 50.53890203369984, "height": 174.56249999999986}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Region pea....", "bbox": {"x": 657.0055499254029, "y": 1883.4374977031252, "width": 27.56667762067581, "height": 137.8125}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Region ends...", "bbox": {"x": 872.9444366043463, "y": 1888.0312483347655, "width": 22.97223536703327, "height": 133.21875000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Tier 1", "bbox": {"x": 422.68888652579545, "y": 1722.656249196094, "width": 22.97222660382582, "height": 64.31250000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "\"Clear distinction\"", "bbox": {"x": 473.2277708225019, "y": 1612.406247090625, "width": 22.97223536703327, "height": 174.5